w:ctm-page-edit
    isa s:kind-deliverable ;
    - "One Item of the CTM plan page edited through HyperDoc" ;
    s:work-status: "open" ;
    s:declaration-text: "One Item of the CTM plan page edited through HyperDoc — the defined scope." .

w:ctm-wp-1
    isa s:kind-work-package ;
    - "Verified page source" ;
    s:work-status: "verified" ;
    s:declaration-text: "Verified page source — WBS 1." ;
    s:wbs-scope: "Observe the page ctm-and-tmdm-in-hyperdoc at the site root of the HyperDoc instance that will edit it, through the existing local site reader (read-local-fedwiki-page, configured-local-site-root), and record site id, site root, slug, page SHA-256 and the Item ids of its story." ;
    s:wbs-acceptance-criterion: "The site root is the one the editing instance is configured with; the slug is a valid page slug; the Item to be edited occurs exactly once; the page digest is recorded, and any difference from the last local observation is explained (for example a fork entry added by the transfer)." ;
    s:wbs-authority: "None to write. Reading the site root needs only the file access the instance already has. The transfer itself is the operator's." ;
    s:wbs-effect: "None: read-only observation." ;
    s:wbs-evidence: "An observation record with site root, slug, digest and Item ids, read in the instance that will perform the edit." .

w:ctm-wp-2
    isa s:kind-work-package ;
    - "Inspectable edit proposal" ;
    s:work-status: "open" ;
    s:declaration-text: "Inspectable edit proposal — WBS 2." ;
    s:wbs-scope: "Form, inside the HyperDoc Inspector, the expected Item (the exact current JSON of the one Item), its replacement with the same id, and the ordinary FedWiki edit Action, bound to the page digest of package 1. Show all three without executing anything. Implemented by item-edit-proposal and item-edit-preview, reached from the Story Item's Edit tab (Prepare edit proposal, Preview, Action context)." ;
    s:wbs-acceptance-criterion: "The replacement keeps the Item id; an unchanged replacement is answered as no change, not as an error; the proposal names the digest it was formed against and a page file that has changed since is refused as stale; for a productive edit the content was decided by a person and that decision is recorded." ;
    s:wbs-authority: "None to prepare. The content decision belongs to the user." ;
    s:wbs-effect: "None: an unexecuted proposal." ;
    s:wbs-evidence: "The proposal and preview objects in the Inspector, with the tests dreyeck/tests/fedwiki-item-edit-preview.lisp, dreyeck/tests/work-item-edit-proposal.lisp and the browser scripts scripts/test-item-edit-proposal.mjs and scripts/test-item-edit-preview-outcomes.mjs; for a productive edit, the recorded content decision." .

w:ctm-wp-3
    isa s:kind-work-package ;
    - "Authorized single-item edit" ;
    s:work-status: "open" ;
    s:declaration-text: "Authorized single-item edit — WBS 3." ;
    s:wbs-scope: "Execute exactly the proposal of package 2 with the existing M0 writer edit-fedwiki-page-item, holding a page-authoring capability for this site root, this page and the Action edit. In production that capability is derived by the existing authenticated path from a signed envelope, a registered principal, a single-use challenge and an authoring rule. Implemented by execute-completed-edit, which first needs the Action completed with a date (complete-item-edit) and a signed request attached by trusted code (attach-signed-request)." ;
    s:wbs-acceptance-criterion: "The writer returns its edit record; nothing is executed without a capability that covers the page and the Action; a page that no longer holds the expected Item is refused as stale; the journal gains exactly this Action. What the execution yields follows the page file read again, not the signalled condition, and three statements stay apart: how the file compares with the preview, the condition of the run, and whom the write is ascribed to." ;
    s:wbs-authority: "A page-authoring capability for site dreyeck.ch, page ctm-and-tmdm-in-hyperdoc, Action edit, derived from an authenticated principal's authoring rule. Not granted. Opening a pane or loading the execution system grants nothing; no Inspector control signs." ;
    s:wbs-effect: "One FedWiki edit Action on one Item of one page." ;
    s:wbs-evidence: "The writer's edit record where it returned, the item-edit-execution with the page file read again, and the authoring request's observation; tested by dreyeck/tests/fedwiki-item-edit-execution.lisp and scripts/test-item-edit-execution.mjs on temporary copies." .

w:ctm-wp-4
    isa s:kind-work-package ;
    - "Verified persisted result" ;
    s:work-status: "open" ;
    s:declaration-text: "Verified persisted result — WBS 4." ;
    s:wbs-scope: "After the effect, read the page again in a fresh process and compare it with the proposal and with the observation of package 1: the same Items in the same order, the edited Item equal to the replacement, every other Item unchanged, the journal extended by exactly the Action. Implemented by verify-persisted-edit, a new SBCL process that loads only shasht and ironclad." ;
    s:wbs-acceptance-criterion: "All comparisons hold. A mismatch is reported as unverified and is not repaired or retried automatically. A file that differs from the preview is never shown as verified; verified states the file, not that the run was clean or that this call wrote it." ;
    s:wbs-authority: "None to write: an independent observation." ;
    s:wbs-effect: "None: read-only verification." ;
    s:wbs-evidence: "An execution-verification-object with the page digest after and the result of each comparison." .

w:ctm-wp-5
    isa s:kind-work-package ;
    - "HyperDoc work evidence" ;
    s:work-status: "open" ;
    s:declaration-text: "HyperDoc work evidence — WBS 5." ;
    s:wbs-scope: "Record the outcome in HyperDoc: change the statuses of the work packages and plan steps on Authoring the CTM Plan Page through the existing Change work status operation, and link the evidence of packages 1 to 4." ;
    s:wbs-acceptance-criterion: "Each status change goes through the existing operation on its exact declaration and is verified by reading the page again; every evidence link resolves; no planning relation is read as an authorization." ;
    s:wbs-authority: "The local HyperDoc authoring environment for status changes on this HyperDoc page, and the user's decision that a package is verified." ;
    s:wbs-effect: "Work status changes on this HyperDoc page only." ;
    s:wbs-evidence: "The Work projection of Authoring the CTM Plan Page after the changes, and the commit that records them." .

