<tag:dreyeck.ch,2026:hyperdoc/assignment/cc-2026-10-18-project-work-ctm>
    isa s:implementation-assignment ;
    - "Claude Code: Project Work as an Exchangeable CTM Topic Map" ;
    s:issued: "Given by the user on 2026-10-18 in a Claude Code session (Claude Opus 5.5, high effort), after an architecture review of CTM roundtrips in HyperDoc." ;
    s:goal: "Show the declared Work Breakdown and project plan of HyperDoc as one CTM Topic Map: derived from the Work pages, read back with the topic-maps reader, navigable in a HyperDoc Project Workspace, and exported as a CTM file that other Topic Maps authors can read without HyperDoc." ;
    s:plan-step-note: "No Plan Step is confirmed for this assignment. Its text cannot make one." ;
    s:observed-state: "Reported by the executor: implemented in the working tree and not committed. On 2026-10-19, with topic-maps 5a4a668, the executor ran the source and read-back tests of dreyeck/work/project, the HyperDoc suites topic-maps-reading, tmdm-reading, item-edit-ctm, ctm-page-authoring, work/reading and dita-story-item, the topic-maps suite, and the browser navigation test in an isolated Catalog; all passed. The counts are in the session report. This report is not an acceptance." ;
    s:acceptance: "No acceptance by the user is recorded." ;
    s:precondition: "A clean topic-maps checkout at 963f2a0 (Slice 17B) in the ASDF registry; the reader is not packaged." ;
    s:precondition: "No commit, push, deployment or SSH; no wiki file is written." ;
    s:precondition: "The Work pages stay authoritative; the CTM is derived from them and changes nothing on them." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "The CTM file is read by the topic-maps reader." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Its Topics have identifiers that depend neither on names nor on positions." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Every Work Topic and statement in it is traced to its declaration, and every declaration is in it." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "WBS decomposition and plan dependencies stay distinct Association types with their own Role types." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "An unchanged export is byte-identical to the imported file; a semantically changed file is recognized through CXTM." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "An unsupported or invalid CTM file is refused with its reason." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "In a local Catalog the Project Workspace leads from the project to a Work Item, its Work Package and a Plan Step, and to source and evidence." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "No wiki file is changed." ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads the Work Breakdown, authoritative for its Work declarations" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads the CTM plan page, authoritative for its WBS, plan steps and preconditions" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads the WBS Dictionary, authoritative for scope, acceptance criteria, authority, effect, evidence and controls" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads this page, authoritative for assignments and proposals" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the Work CTM emitter" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the import, comparison and the Project Workspace" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the derived CTM document" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the Catalog entry page" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds this page" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the systems dreyeck/work/project and dreyeck/work/project/tests" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the digest of the derived CTM document, kept beside it" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the tests of the emitter, the read-back, the comparison, the export and the Workspace" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds a loopback review Catalog over a temporary test copy" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the browser navigation test in that isolated Catalog" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "names the topic-maps revision HyperDoc is tested with" ;
    s:evidence-note: "Lisp tests of system dreyeck/work/project/tests" ;
    s:evidence-note: "browser navigation in an isolated Catalog with a temporary copy" .

