<tag:dreyeck.ch,2026:hyperdoc/assignment/cc-2026-10-19-topic-maps-reader-scaling>
    isa s:implementation-assignment ;
    - "Claude Code: Read the complete project CTM in practical time" ;
    s:issued: "Given by the user on 2026-10-19 in the same Claude Code session (Claude Opus 5.5, high effort), after the topic-maps reader of 963f2a0 did not read the generated project CTM: fix its scaling as a slice of its own in the topic-maps repository, with its test suite as the gate." ;
    s:goal: "Read the complete project CTM with the topic-maps reader in practical time, without weakening TMDM semantics, so that the project CTM can be read back, compared and navigated." ;
    s:plan-step-note: "No Plan Step is confirmed for this assignment. Its text cannot make one." ;
    s:observed-state: "Reported by the executor: committed in topic-maps as 5a4a668 after the user approved the commit; HyperDoc's dependency was updated to it after the user approved the update, both on 2026-10-19. Not pushed. This report is not an acceptance." ;
    s:acceptance: "No acceptance by the user is recorded." ;
    s:precondition: "No change to the pinned checkout topic-maps-hyperdoc; no push, deployment or SSH; no commit without the user's approval." ;
    s:precondition: "The emitter, its identities and the project model are not changed to accommodate the reader." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "The complete project CTM is read correctly in practical time." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Merge and reification semantics are unchanged: regression tests recorded with the unchanged 963f2a0 before the change pass after it." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "The complete topic-maps test suite passes with outputs equal to the 963f2a0 run." ;
    s:source-authority-note: "topic-maps 963f2a0 (Slice 17B), the reference implementation; its checkout topic-maps-hyperdoc is not changed" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "topic-maps src/tmdm/merging.lisp and src/tmdm/associations.lisp, changed in the separate worktree topic-maps-normalization" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "records the topic-maps revision HyperDoc is tested with and shows the loaded reader's source identity" ;
    s:evidence-note: "topic-maps commit 5a4a668 on branch claude/ctm-reader-normalization-scaling: EQUAL-TOPIC-PAIR and EQUAL-ASSOCIATION-PAIR return the pairs EQUAL-PAIR returns, through an index" ;
    s:evidence-note: "topic-maps suite in its pinned shell, on the clean commit: exit 0; every PASS line and all 20 report files equal to the 963f2a0 run; NORMALIZATION-PASS 77 checks" ;
    s:evidence-note: "differential: 273 corpus files with equal outcomes; equal CXTM on every benchmark input the unchanged reader completed" ;
    s:evidence-note: "complete project CTM: 7.4 s with the correction; the unchanged reader did not complete within 300 s" ;
    s:evidence-note: "HyperDoc read-back of the complete project CTM with the pinned revision" .

<tag:dreyeck.ch,2026:hyperdoc/assignment/cc-2026-10-19-acceptance-model-draft>
    isa s:implementation-assignment ;
    - "Claude Code: Work Package, Evidence and Acceptance (draft)" ;
    s:issued: "Given by the user on 2026-10-19 in the same Claude Code session (Claude Opus 5.5), after the walk of the Project Workspace showed that pwc-wp-8 has no evidence or acceptance of its own: prepare an explicit acceptance concept that the project CTM can state, without recording any acceptance." ;
    s:goal: "Make three things distinguishable and navigable: a work package with its acceptance criterion and required evidence, an implementation assignment with its observed evidence and result, and an acceptance record with its decision, deciding authority and the evidence it considered. Demonstrate the record only on a synthetic fixture; record no acceptance of pwc-wp-8." ;
    s:plan-step-note: "No Plan Step is confirmed for this assignment. Its text cannot make one." ;
    s:observed-state: "Reported by the executor: a draft in the working tree, not committed. The draft pages are not sources of the project CTM; making them sources is the user's decision. This report is not an acceptance." ;
    s:acceptance: "No acceptance by the user is recorded." ;
    s:precondition: "No acceptance is recorded for pwc-wp-8 or any other package; the record form is shown only on a synthetic fixture." ;
    s:precondition: "Existing subject identifiers and Work relations stay unchanged; no Work declaration changes." ;
    s:precondition: "No commit, push or deployment without the user's approval." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Work package, implementation assignment and acceptance record stay distinguishable." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Required evidence is not given out as observed evidence." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "An assignment's evidence does not become a work package's acceptance." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "No acceptance record exists without an explicitly declared decision." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "Subject identifiers and existing Work relations are preserved." ;
    s:acceptance-criterion: "The CTM is reproducible and its projection in the Inspector traceable." ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads the produces contract and the declared work packages" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads the form of a WBS Dictionary entry: scope, acceptance criterion, authority, effect, required evidence, controls" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds a draft WBS Dictionary for project-work-ctm-exchange; not a source of the project CTM until the user decides" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds a draft Acceptance Records page without records; not a source of the project CTM until the user decides" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "reads a draft dictionary and an Acceptance Records page when they are sources, and writes their vocabulary only then" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "shows acceptance records, criteria and authorities in the Workspace" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the acceptance tests" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "adds the synthetic fixture, whose identifiers all start with synthetic-" ;
    s:source-authority-note: "states the proposal and the decisions it needs" ;
    s:evidence-note: "acceptance tests of system dreyeck/work/project/tests, on the synthetic fixture and on the drafts" .

